{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDQ67JoN1UWNJEdRtAN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the two screens, each sent through `Analytics.capture`. `dart format` and `flutter analyze` report no issues. I haven't run the app (the repo has no tests), so no events have actually been sent to PostHog yet.\n\n**Registration screen (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`):**\n- **Email and phone \"started\" events:** each fires the first time its field has text, once per visit to the screen. They don't fire on every keystroke, and the email and phone text are never sent.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** fires when the user lets go of the slider, with the rounded amount. The normal slider callback fires on every frame of a drag, which would use up the free-tier event allowance fast.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** fires only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** fires before going to the offers screen, with `amount` and `terms`. `terms` will always be `true` here, because Continue can only be tapped once terms are accepted.\n\n**Offers screen (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`):**\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** fires each time a scroll comes to rest, with the offset, rather than on every scroll update.\n- **Possible gap:** there are only 10 offers, so on tall screens the list may not scroll at all. That would make this last funnel step look smaller than it really is.\n\nWhile checking the code, `flutter analyze` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml` by itself, so I put it back. I also deleted the `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/` that the tooling created. The only changes now are the two screen files and `ANSWER.md`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":28658,"cache_creation":{"e